A||||6||fierocd||fuel pump help||||5||
Z||000000||fierocd||08-26-2001||12:39 PM||||OK, I got my car running normal again, but now I think my fuel pump is shot.  The car still doesn't seem to have much power and I can hear all kinds of noises comming from the fuel pump.  It also decides to come on whenever it wants now - with the car turned off(oil pressure sending unit is only 2 months old). Should I get the fuel pump at Autozone for $49, or take the fuel pump out of my parts car and use that one?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mach10||08-26-2001||12:51 PM||||Can you spare the $50? If you can, there's no reason not to go with a new one. On the other hand, the other pump may be good for a while yet, and $50 will get you a lot of beer...<P><BR>MMmmmmmm... Beer... gragghhhhhhhhh.||||reg||10
Z||000002||fierocd||08-26-2001||01:14 PM||||How hard is the fuel pump to change when the gas tank is full?||||reg||1
Z||000003||starfighter007@msn.com||08-26-2001||01:41 PM||||Never done it with a full tank .But if you dont get that gas out or at least most of it you will have a big mess to deal with. It will be a lot easier to manage with most of the gas out ||||reg||7
Z||000004||fierocd||08-26-2001||02:09 PM||||What is the best/easiest way to get the gas out?||||reg||1
Z||000005||LivoniaFieroGT||08-26-2001||04:52 PM||||I took the feed line off, patched a 5 foot line on and pumped the gas into my wife's Trans Sport using the intank pump.  If yours has failed completely, cannot help.  Maybe use an inline pump off to the side.  The old racing electric pumps.  Otherwise at 7lbs per gallon.... that's gonna be one heavy tank to drop.<BR>You will need a 13mm long deepwell socket. I thought I had about ever size socket there was but had to buy a 2 1/2" deepwell to reach way in there. And then it only just made it.   good luck<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierocd||08-26-2001||11:20 PM||||Thanks for the help, I just took a long hose and syphoned about 5 gallons out.  Then when I got the tank out I poured out the rest of the gas to make it easier to put back in.  The car started right up and seemed fine when I took it for a test drive.||||reg||1
